Power of Government to make rules

ACT V OF 1987
ACT V OF 1987
SIND MEDICAL COLLEGES ACT, 1987
3. Power of Government to make
rules.‑‑(1) Notwithstanding anything contained in any law, for the
time being in force, but subject to the Medical Councils Ordinance, 1962,
Government may by rules‑‑
(a) regulate admissions in a medical college;
(b) supervise and control
discipline of students;
(c) institute, maintain and
control halls of residence and approve any place as hostel or lodging for
students.
(2) Without prejudice to the
generally of the foregoing provisions, the rules may provide for‑‑
(a) allocation of seats;
(b) form of application for admission;
(c) conditions for admission;
(d) conditions for and procedure of migration;
(e) disciplinary action against and imposition of penalty on students;
(f) institution and maintenance
of and conditions for admission to the residential halls and hostels.
